utional policies and procedures Communicate with department leadership as needed Stay current in subject area and teaching practices Qualifications Ph.D. or D.B.A. in Business or a related discipline is required. Prior college-level teaching experience Relevant professional experience in the field Basic proficiency with instructional technology and learning management systems (i.e. Canvas) Application Requirements Applicants must submit the following materials: Current curriculum vitae List of courses taught, including dates and institutions Transcripts from all degree-granting institutions (official copies required upon hiring) Contact information for three (3) professional references (references will not be contacted without prior notification) EEO Statement: Wheeling University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to creating and sustaining a diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all faculty, staff, and students. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. We value the unique contributions that individuals bring to our campus and believe that diversity of perspectives enriches our academic and work environment. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
