    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/B369DDFCCC4F5E809A5BFCBD09E2C573/jobs/292946": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Nursing",
      "description": "Adjunct, Nursing You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct, Nursing Wheeling University - Wheeling, WV 26003 Apply Overview Position Type Seasonal Category Education Apply Description At Wheeling University, you’ll find more than just a workplace — you’ll join a mission-driven community that lives by values of leadership, service, faith, integrity, and excellence . As an employee, you’ll be part of a university that is committed to integrating learning, research, and outreach within its Catholic tradition, seeking to develop not only competent professionals, but also socially responsible citizens. Wheeling promotes close student-faculty connections and encourages all members to grow both intellectually and ethically, to serve with compassion among diverse communities, and to lead by example. In such an environment, your work will matter — your contributions help sustain a culture where academic rigor, moral purpose, and service to others are not just ideals, but daily practice. Wheeling University is seeking an Adjunct Professor for their Nursing Program to start in the Spring of 2027! The ideal candidate would be able to teach courses at the Master’s of Nursing level and the Bachelors of Nursing level. Responsibilities : Each assigned undergraduate and/or graduate nursing didactic courses in an online learning environment. Prepare for and facilitate assigned courses in accordance with approved course syllabi, curriculum requirements, course learning outcomes, and program outcomes. Maintain an active and consistent faculty presence within the online learning environment. Communicate course expectations, assignments, grading criteria, and academic requirements clearly to students. Provide timely, substantive, and constructive feedback on student assignments, examinations, discussions, and other learning activities. Grade student work consistently and in accordance with established grading rubrics, course policies, and Nursing Program policies. Monitor student academic progress and communicate concerns regarding student performance in a timely manner. Provide appropriate academic support and guidance to students and refer students to University resources when additional assistance is needed. Facilitate online discussions and learning activities that promote critical thinking, clinical judgment, evidence-based practice, professional communication, and application of nursing knowledge. Utilize current evidence, professional nursing standards, and best practices in nursing education when facilitating course content. Maintain current knowledge within the instructor's assigned area of nursing practice and education. Utilize the University's learning management system and other approved instructional technologies effectively. Maintain accurate and timely course records, including grades, attendance or participation documentation when applicable, and student communications. Respond to student communications within established Nursing Program and University expectations. Participate in course and program assessment activities, including evaluation of student learning outcomes and collection of assessment data as requested. Identify opportunities for course improvement and communicate recommendations to nursing program leadership. Participate in orientation, faculty development, and training related to online instruction, instructional technology, assessment, academic integrity, and University policies. Follow University and Nursing Program policies regarding academic integrity, student confidentiality, accessibility, grading, and professional conduct. Maintain student educational records in accordance with FERPA and applicable University policies. Participate in faculty meetings, committee activities, program evaluation, accreditation activities, and other Nursing Program responsibilities as assigned. Collaborate professionally with nursing faculty, program leadership, academic support personnel, and other University departments. Complete required University and Nursing Program documentation by established deadlines. Perform other duties consistent with the faculty role as assigned by the Chair of Nursing or appropriate academic administrator. Qualifications Qualifications are congruent with the qualifications of nursing faculty as required by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education. Have a graduate degree with a major in nursing Holds a current, active RN license or privilege to practice that is not encumbered and meets the requirements of the Board of Nursing. EEO Statement: Wheeling University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to creating and sustaining a diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all faculty, staff, and students. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. We value the unique contributions that individuals bring to our campus and believe that diversity of perspectives enriches our academic and work environment. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
