    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/B369DDFCCC4F5E809A5BFCBD09E2C573/jobs/291012": {
      "title": "Accountant",
      "description": "Accountant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Accountant Wheeling University - Wheeling, WV 26003 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Employment Education Level 4 Year Degree Category Education Apply Description At Wheeling University, you’ll find more than just a workplace — you’ll join a mission-driven community that lives by values of leadership, service, faith, integrity, and excellence . As an employee, you’ll be part of a university that is committed to integrating learning, research, and outreach within its Catholic tradition, seeking to develop not only competent professionals, and also socially responsible citizens. Wheeling promotes close student-faculty connections and encourages all members to grow both intellectually and ethically, to serve with compassion among diverse communities, and to lead by example. In such an environment, your work will matter — your contributions help sustain a culture where academic rigor, moral purpose, and service to others are more deals --they are daily actions and practices. Wheeling University is looking for a full-time, onsite Accountant who is responsible for managing and maintaining accurate financial records, preparing reports, and ensuring compliance with accounting principles and company policies. This role supports the organization’s financial health by assisting with budgeting, audits, reconciliations, and general ledger activities. Responsibilities: Prepare and maintain financial records, reports, and statements. Perform general ledger entries, reconciliations, and month-end/year-end closings. Process accounts payable and accounts receivable transactions. Assist in preparing budgets, forecasts, and financial analyses. Ensure compliance with GAAP and relevant laws and regulations. Support internal and external audits by providing necessary documentation. Identify and recommend process improvements to enhance financial accuracy and efficiency. Maintain confidentiality of financial data and company information. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field. One to three years of related experience (higher education experience preferred). Proven experience as an accountant or in a similar role. Strong knowledge of accounting principles and practices. Proficiency in accounting software (e.g., QuickBooks, SAP, NetSuite) and Microsoft Excel. Experience with Ellucian Colleague preferred. Excellent attention to detail and organizational skills. Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Work Environment: Office setting with standard business hours. May require occasional overtime during reporting or audit periods. Wheeling University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to creating and sustaining a diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all faculty, staff, and students. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. We value the unique contributions that individuals bring to our campus and believe that diversity of perspectives enriches our academic and work environment. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
