ovement and growth of the Business programs. Participating in departmental, school, and university committees. Supporting assessment activities and maintaining compliance with ACBSP accreditation standards. Preparing course syllabi and instructional materials. Assessing student learning, assigning grades, and submitting final grades in a timely manner. Conducting end-of-semester course assessments and surveys. Maintaining accurate attendance and course records using Canvas. Holding regular office hours and providing academic support to students. Qualifications Ph.D. or DBA in Business, Business Administration, or a closely related field, or be expected to complete the degree by May 2027. Significant professional experience in higher education teaching Demonstrated commitment to teaching and student success College-level teaching experience Experience with ACBSP-accredited programs Application Requirements Applicants must submit the following materials: Current curriculum vitae A list of courses taught, including dates and institutions Statement of teaching philosophy Transcripts from all degree-granting institutions (official copies required upon hiring) A list of three (3) professional/personal references, including contacts from prior employers listed on the CV (references will not be contacted without prior notification to the candidate) Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. EEO Statement: Wheeling University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to creating and sustaining a diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all faculty, staff, and students. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. We value the unique contributions that individuals bring to our campus and believe that diversity of perspectives enriches our academic and work environment. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
